  "summary": "These passages connect endurance with hardship, hope, and continued faithfulness. Romans 5 describes suffering as producing endurance, character, and hope. Hebrews urges readers to hold firm, continue in confidence, and run with perseverance while looking to Jesus. James 1 says testing can produce endurance and maturity. Together the texts encourage persistence through difficulty, but they address readers in different situations and do not settle every later debate about perseverance.",
  "historical_context": "The references include Paul’s argument in Romans, exhortations in Hebrews, and James’s instruction about trials. The sources are the cited biblical texts; this account stays with their literary and pastoral settings rather than proposing an external historical reconstruction.",
