  "literary_context": "Romans 5 gives a sequence from suffering to hope. Hebrews combines warning and encouragement, culminating in the image of a race. James addresses trials directly and links endurance with maturity. The distinct forms help readers hear the theme without turning it into a single formula.",
  "covenantal_significance": "The cited writings portray endurance as a way of remaining faithful under pressure, grounded in hope and directed toward maturity. Hebrews’ focus on Jesus, Romans’ account of hope, and James’s counsel about testing offer related but distinct reasons to persist.",
